sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (UI)
    participant P as Shielded Pool
    participant R as Relayer / Paymaster
    participant B as Burner EOA
    participant C as HyperCore

    Note over U,C: PHASE 1 — DERIVE · off-chain, nothing touches any chain
    U->>U: burner key = derive(spending key, index i)
    Note over U,B: deterministic, so every burner is recoverable from the seed the user already holds · the UI names it, e.g. BTC-10x-LONG

    Note over U,C: PHASE 2 — FUND · the pool's first of two appearances
    U->>P: shielded WITHDRAW, relayed · target = burner
    Note over P,R: ONE transaction carries BOTH assets: USDC margin + native HYPE for gas · fee paid in-asset via Paymaster
    P->>R: proof + payload (relayer sees burner, amount, time — never the user)
    R->>B: USDC + HYPE land at a fresh address that has touched nothing else
    Note over B: the burner's gas came FROM THE POOL — funding it from the user's wallet is total deanonymisation

    Note over U,C: PHASE 3 — ACTIVATE AND BRIDGE · burner acts alone from here
    B->>C: ERC20 transfer to the Core system address (0x20..00 + tokenIndex)
    C-->>B: spot credited, minus the 1 USDC first-time activation fee
    B->>C: usdClassTransfer(ntl, toPerp = true) · spot becomes perp margin

    Note over U,C: PHASE 4 — TRADE · signed L1 actions, no pool, no contract
    B->>C: updateLeverage(asset, isCross = FALSE, leverage) · genuine isolated margin, per position
    B->>C: place order / cancel / close, signed by the burner key
    Note over B,C: the position is public — size, entry, liquidation on the API and leaderboards, attached to the burner forever

    Note over U,C: PHASE 5 — RETURN · the pool's second appearance · ONE transaction
    B->>C: close position · usdClassTransfer(toPerp = false)
    C-->>B: spot sent back to the burner's EVM balance
    U->>U: app proves a deposit whose output notes are owned by the user's MAIN shielded address
    B->>P: burner submits the PUBLIC deposit — no burner registration, no internal transfer
    P-->>U: notes land directly in the main account, recipient hidden among ALL registered addresses
    Note over B,P: only the AMOUNT leaks — the burner returns a PnL-shaped number (6.2's remaining half)
